{
  "manufacturer": "Trane",
  "manufacturer_slug": "trane",
  "model": "TruSense RMWH refrigerant monitor (up to 16 points)",
  "model_slug": "trusense-rmwh-refrigerant-monitor",
  "short_model": "TruSense RMWH",
  "aliases": [
    "TruSense",
    "RMWH",
    "Trane refrigerant monitor",
    "PART-SVX008A",
    "RMWH-SVX001"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (refrigerant leak monitor for chiller plant rooms)",
  "applies_to": "Trane TruSense RMWH multipoint photoacoustic refrigerant monitor with Modbus RTU selected, per IOM PART-SVX008A-EN (30 Sep 2025, preliminary).",
  "summary": "Wall-mounted sample-draw refrigerant monitor for chiller and equipment rooms that checks up to 16 points for leaks of the common HVAC refrigerants. Over Modbus RTU it exposes 16-bit holding registers: unit status, an acknowledge and reset command, per-channel gas type, ppm reading and alarm flags, and calibration dates.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The register table's 'Index' column prints Modicon holding registers from 40001, so 40001 is wire address 0 and channel 1 gas concentration 40011 is wire address 10."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Installation, Operation, and Maintenance: TruSense RMWH Refrigerant Monitor",
    "doc_number": "PART-SVX008A-EN",
    "revision_date": "2025-09-30",
    "url": "https://elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/commercial-hvac/Literature/Installation%20Operation%20and%20Maintenance/PART-SVX008A-EN_09302025.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 20-21 (digital output setup), pp. 53-56 (Appendix D Modbus holding registers, reset actions, status flags, gas types)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The register list gives no data type or multiplier; every register is one 16-bit word, typed here as unsigned. Concentrations are listed in ppm as printed (the specifications give a 0-1000 ppm range and 1 ppm resolution).",
    "RESET button actions (40009): high byte 0 + channel number (0-15) resets that channel's alarms, 0/255 resets all channel alarms; 1 + channel resets that channel's faults, 1/255 all channel faults; 2/255 resets common faults; 3/255 resets all alarms and faults.",
    "Each channel also has a 'Reserved' register that reads 0 (40013, 40017 ... 40073); these and Reserved 40004-40006 are left out.",
    "The document is marked 'Preliminary' and supersedes RMWH-SVX001D-EN.",
    "Baud rate and device address are chosen on the touchscreen; the manual does not list the defaults, the baud choices or parity.",
    "The table's 'Index' column starts at 40001 in 5-digit Modicon form; the manual gives no separate offset statement, so 40001 is taken as wire address 0."
  ],
